    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=089b582f-0a35-44db-98f2-170a98083ab9&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204937024447_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Hourly Identity Verification and CRM Support",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\n\nHourly Identity Verification and CRM Support Part-Time/Temporary: November through April $25/hour, 15 hours/week Office of the President, CRM Team  111 West State Street, Trenton, NJ 08608 (Primarily Remote with occasional on-site meetings for onboarding and implementation)  Thomas Edison State University was founded in 1972 to break down barriers to degree completion. Fifty years later, it proudly serves a diverse body of adult students with innovative and professionally relevant academic programming in a predominantly online delivery. Our team of high-energy student-focused professionals is welcoming new members who are making their mark in education and are ready to help change the lives of thousands of adult students across New Jersey and around the world. Candidates who are excited by changing lives, committed to the success of all and want to be challenged by new and innovative opportunities, should submit an application.   Summary: Reporting to the Associate Director of CRM Operations, the Hourly Identity Verification & CRM Support position will assist the CRM technical team with application processing, identity verification protocols, and routine CRM tasks. This role ensures operational continuity, maintains rigorous fraud prevention standards, and preserves prompt turnaround times during peak admissions cycles and the winter closure period, allowing core technical staff to focus on complex enterprise CRM implementation milestones. Key Responsibilities: - Application Processing: Reviewing, processing, and maintaining new undergraduate applications to ensure prompt turnaround times and continuous operational flow. - Fraud Reviews & Identity Verification: Executing identity verification and fraud review protocols to safeguard the integrity of admissions procedures and protect institutional security. - Zendesk Ticket Responses: Providing timely, accurate support and resolving applicant inquiries submitted through Zendesk support channels. - Winter Break Continuity: Maintaining continuous departmental operations and application reviews during TESU’s winter break (December 24 th through January 4 th ).   Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: - Technical Proficiency: Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and modern CRM environments.  - Organizational Skills: Proven attention to detail, exceptional organizational skills, and the ability to work independently and consistently meet deadlines.  - Communication: Outstanding oral and written communication skills with a customer service-oriented, positive attitude.  - Confidentiality & Inclusion: Ability to handle sensitive information confidentially and interact positively and professionally with diverse groups.   Requirements: Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university.  Experience: Relevant work experience with higher education admissions technology, including Recruit CRM and other Ellucian products, and identity verification software.    *TESU strives to offer a flexible work environment while balancing the operational needs of the University. As such, we have several options for hybrid-work schedules. Positions determine what type of hybrid-work schedule is available and, if necessary, adjustments are made to support University operations.    Thomas Edison State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=089b582f-0a35-44db-98f2-170a98083ab9&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204897198343_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Hourly Nursing Prerequisite Course Navigator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\n\nLocation: Trenton\n\nHourly Nursing Prerequisite Course Navigator Part-Time/Hourly: $40/hour, 25 hours/week Office of Strategic Initiatives and Institutional Effectiveness 301 West State Street Trenton, NJ 08618   Thomas Edison State University was founded in 1972 to break down barriers to degree completion. Fifty years later, it proudly serves a diverse body of adult students with innovative and professionally relevant academic programming in a predominantly online delivery. Our team of high-energy student-focused professionals is welcoming new members who are making their mark in education and are ready to help change the lives of thousands of adult students across New Jersey and around the world. Candidates who are excited by changing lives, committed to the success of all and want to be challenged by new and innovative opportunities, should submit an application. Summary:   The hourly Nursing Prerequisite Course Navigator serves in a pivotal role to connect, track, and support Accelerated Baccalaureate Nursing (BSNA) applicants through their journey of prerequisite course completion. This position reports to the Assistant Director of Strategic Initiatives and will connect Admissions, the W. Cary Edwards School of Nursing, and the Office of the Registrar staff with information regarding applicants’ progression towards their BSNA application. Job Duties:   -Manage a caseload of BSNA applicants who need to complete prerequisite courses (not GE). -Track all BSNA applicants from the first advising appointment through prerequisite completion on a spreadsheet. -Direct BSNA applicants to review the Office of the Registrar's initial program evaluation. -Answer routine applicant questions about approved prerequisite courses options.  -Record prerequisite course completion on the BSNA Tracking Unity Form in OnBase. -Inform BSNA applicants of process to have official transcripts sent to Office of the Registrar and verify receipt in Colleague XIA. -Track prerequisite course completion for reporting to various departments to determine progression toward BSNA application readiness. -Prioritize TESU’s 4-Week Accelerated Terms/Courses. -Communicate proactively with BSNA applicants as they complete prerequisite courses, sharing a prerequisite completion task list w/ periodic check-ins and updates. -Check-ins and updates with applicants should occur following a timeline appropriate to the applicant’s prerequisite course completion plan.  -As applicants complete all prerequisite course(s), notify the Office of the Registrar and the nursing advisors for application decisions. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities:   - Knowledge of the principles and techniques essential to perform assigned responsibilities. - Experience in healthcare preferred. - Enhanced customer service knowledge. - Ability to acquire extensive knowledge of university policies and procedures, especially those related to course evaluation. - Ability to understand, interpret, and apply established procedures, and guidelines. - Ability to counsel potential BSNA applicants and others concerning prerequisite courses. - Excellent verbal and written communication skills. - Ability to work well with others in a team environment - Ability to maintain essential records and files. - Expert knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite including Excel Working knowledge of Student Information Systems or the ability to learn them quickly Knowledge of FERPA and the ability to maintain the confidentiality of student records - Excellent organizational skills. - Attention to detail - Take on other responsibilities as assigned.   Qualifications:   Education: - Baccalaureate degree   *TESU strives to offer a flexible work environment while balancing the operational needs of the University. As such, we have several options for hybrid-work schedules. Positions determine what type of hybrid-work schedule is available and, if necessary, adjustments are made to support University operations.    Thomas Edison State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=089b582f-0a35-44db-98f2-170a98083ab9&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204665775514_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "National Test Ctr Coord/RBR, Charleston AFB",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\n\nLocation: Trenton\n\nNational Test Center Coordinator/Regional Base Representative, Charleston AFB  Hourly/Part-Time: $30/hour 25 hours/week  Office of Military and Veteran Enrollment and Outreach  Naval Weapons Station/Naval Consolidated Brig, Charleston, South Carolina, US  Thomas Edison State University was founded in 1972 to break down barriers to degree completion. Fifty years later, it proudly serves a diverse body of adult students with innovative and professionally relevant academic programming in a predominantly online delivery. Our team of high-energy student-focused professionals is welcoming new members who are making their mark in education and are ready to help change the lives of thousands of adult students across New Jersey and around the world. Candidates who are excited by changing lives, committed to the success of all and want to be challenged by new and innovative opportunities, should submit an application.   Job Summary:  Under the supervision of the Associate Director of Military and Veteran Admissions and Enrollment Services , the National Test Center Coordinator/Regional Base Representative fulfills a professional role in support of the University’s national test center and the onboarding and evolution of the relationship with its students. The National Test Center Coordinator/Regional Base Representative is responsible for scheduling, administering, and proctoring various tests available for students at the national test center, and assisting with basic recruitment and administrative functions and activities involved in each phase of the student’s application and enrollment process with the University. General responsibilities include responding to telephone and e-mail inquiries regarding testing, admission, application and enrollment policies and procedures, initial financial aid counseling, course registration and navigation, as well as conducting telephone follow-up and outreach recruitment activities.   Knowledge, Skills & Abilities:  - Knowledge of the principles and techniques essential to perform assigned responsibilities. - Enhanced customer service knowledge. - Basic knowledge of admissions and recruitment procedures. - Ability to acquire extensive knowledge of University policies and procedures, especially those related to non-traditional adult higher education. - Ability to understand, analyze, interpret and apply established law, regulations, procedures, precedents and guidelines. - Ability to counsel students and others concerning University programs, activities and services. - Ability to establish cooperative working relationships and coordinate with other offices or organizations that impact assigned responsibilities. - Ability to represent the University by participating in or speaking at conferences, education fairs, meetings, seminars, etc. - Ability to prepare clear, technically sound, accurate and informative reports containing findings, conclusions, and recommendations. - Excellent verbal and written communication skills. - Ability to maintain essential records and files.   Examples of Work:  - Schedule and Proctor tests and exams at the national test center. - Respond to telephone inquiries. - Respond to e-mail inquiries. - Provide excellent customer service to students over the phone and via email. - Participate in telephone outbound follow-up and marketing efforts. - Participate in University outreach recruitment activities. - Participate and complete work through the University CRM and Help Desk ticket system. - Prepare clear and concise statistical and interpretative reports on various metrics, when assigned. - Process student registration and payments, as needed. - Handle basic technical support issues. - Assist in resolving student issues involving: testing, admissions, registration, financial aid, and other student-facing offices. - Assumes other responsibilities as assigned by the Associate Director of Military and Veteran Enrollment and Outreach.   Requirements:  Education: Graduation from an accredited college with a Bachelor's degree. Experience: One (1) year of professional experience in an institution of higher education or in education, higher education or other field that directly relates to the functions of the position, or equivalency as determined by the appointing authority. - The minimum education experience standards for positions classified under this class title will vary depending upon the requirements of the specific position. In each case, these minimums will be determined at the discretion of the appointing authority. - Applicants who do not possess the required education may substitute required experience on a year-for-year basis (30 credit hours is considered one year of college). - A Master's degree in a field related to the position may be substituted for one year of the required experience. - Preferred experience working with military-affiliated and veteran students.   Work Hours:    To be determined; up to 25 hours a week. *TESU strives to offer a flexible work environment while balancing the operational needs of the University. As such, we have several options for hybrid-work schedules. Positions determine what type of hybrid-work schedule is available and, if necessary, adjustments are made to support University operations.   Thomas Edison State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=089b582f-0a35-44db-98f2-170a98083ab9&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9204704558394_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Regional Base Representative, Jacksonville FL",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\n\nRegional Base Representative Part-Time Hourly/Temporary: $30/hour 25 hours/week  Office of Military and Veteran Enrollment and Outreach Jacksonville, FL Thomas Edison State University was founded in 1972 to break down barriers to degree completion. Fifty years later, it proudly serves a diverse body of adult students with innovative and professionally relevant academic programming in a predominantly online delivery. Our team of high-energy student-focused professionals is welcoming new members who are making their mark in education and are ready to help change the lives of thousands of adult students across New Jersey and around the world. Candidates who are excited by changing lives, committed to the success of all and want to be challenged by new and innovative opportunities, should submit an application.   Summary:   Under the supervision of the Associate Director of Military and Veteran Admissions and Enrollment Services, the Regional Base Representative fulfills an important role in support of the University’s Military and Veteran Admissions and Enrollment Services Team and is responsible for assisting students and staff with the basic administrative functions and activities involved in each phase of the student’s application and enrollment process with the University. General responsibilities include responding to telephone and e-mail inquiries regarding admissions and enrollment policies and procedures, course registration and navigation, as well as other administrative functions related to earning a degree with the University. The Regional Base Representative will assist the Associate Director of Military and Veteran Admissions and Enrollment Services and team with additional responsibilities as required.    Knowledge, Skills & Abilities:   - Knowledge of the principles and techniques essential to perform assigned responsibilities.  - Enhanced customer service knowledge. - Ability to acquire extensive knowledge of University policies and procedures. - Ability to coordinate office operations.  - Ability to assist in establishing systems and procedures. - Ability to understand, analyze, interpret, and apply established law, regulations, procedures,  precedents and guidelines.  - Ability to interpret and counsel students and others concerning University programs, tuition,  financial aid, the University evaluation tool, Learning Management System, myEdison, as well  as various other activities and services.  - Ability to interpret and utilize the Recruit, Colleague, and Help Desk ticket platforms as it  pertains to daily and departmental responsibilities. - Ability to establish and lead cooperative working relationships and coordinate with other  offices or organizations that impact assigned responsibilities.  - Ability to represent the University by participating in or speaking at conferences, meetings, and  seminars.  - Ability to prepare clear, technically sound, accurate and informative reports containing  findings, conclusions, and recommendations.  - Ability to prepare correspondence.  - Ability to maintain essential records and files.    Primary Responsibilities: - Increase new military-affiliated student enrollments. - Increase reenrolled military-affiliated student enrollments. - Schedule and present monthly admitted not registered webinars for students in assigned Recruit  CRM territories. - Assist new students with the application and registration process at the University. - Conduct pre-enrollment counseling to guide new prospective students and applicants. - Guide returning inactive students through the reenrollment process at the University. - Participate and complete work through Colleague, Recruit CRM, and Help Desk ticket system. - Respond to and follow up on student inquiries through University phone system. - Respond to and follow up on student email requests and inquiries. - Assist in resolving student issues, when necessary, involving: admissions, registration, financial  aid, testing and other student-facing offices. - Upon evaluation completion, provide via email, a personalized email to new students that  includes degree specific information, including two course recommendations. - Investigate administrative and organizational problems and assists in developing and  implementing solutions to help achieve organizational goals. - Work cooperatively with employees of the University and other organizations while  performing assigned responsibilities. - Prepare reports as required by the Associate Director of Military and Veteran Admissions and  Enrollment Services. - Assume other responsibilities as assigned by the Associate Director of Military and  Veteran Admissions and Enrollment Services.  Requirements:    Education: Graduation from an accredited college with a bachelor's degree.  Experience: One (1) year of professional experience in an institution of higher education or in education, higher education or other field that directly relates to the functions of the position, or equivalency as determined by the appointing authority.  - The minimum education experience standards for positions classified under this class title will vary depending upon the requirements of the specific position. In each case, these minimums will be determined at the discretion of the appointing authority.  - Applicants who do not possess the required education may substitute required experience on a year-for-year basis (30 credit hours is considered one year of college).  - A master's degree in a field related to the position may be substituted for one year of the required experience. - Preferred experience working with military-affiliated and veteran students.  Work Hours: TBD: Part-Time Hourly, 25 Hours Per Week Additional hours, occasionally beyond posted University working hours are necessary to provide assistance at University Recruitment and Outreach events. Thomas Edison State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer",
